# Every text file comes out of git ending its lines with "\n", on every
# system. Git for Windows, left to itself, hands them out with "\r\n", and
# Longhand counts on the bytes: a prompt's fingerprint is taken from its
# file as it lies (agent/longhand-agent, `prompt_version`), and the shell
# scripts are run by a bash that reads "\r" as part of a word. Found by the
# suite's first run on a Windows machine of GitHub's (tests/test_line_endings.py).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fonts are bytes, never lines.
*.ttf binary
